# Shell environment (agent execution)

James's login shell sources `~/.aliases`, `~/.environment`, and `~/.git-safe-force-push.sh`. Agent terminals are often read-only to the user while a command runs.

## Interactive aliases (will hang)

`rm`, `cp`, and `mv` are aliased to `*-i` in `~/.aliases`. In non-interactive or agent shells:

- Use `command rm`, `rm -f`, `git mv`, or `/bin/cp` — not bare `rm` after `cp`.
- Never chain `cp … && rm …` without `rm -f` (macOS `rm -i` blocks on confirmation).

## Git

- Use `git --no-pager` (or `GIT_PAGER=cat`) when parsing output in scripts.
- Do not use `git ci` — global alias is `commit -a` (commits all tracked changes).
- `git push --force` / `git push -f` is rewritten to `--force-with-lease --force-if-includes` via `~/.git-safe-force-push.sh`.
- Avoid `git ui` (opens `tig`). Avoid repo git aliases `.gr` (mass-deletes untracked) and `.gd` (`git delete`).

For automated commits, use `GIT_EDITOR=true` or `git commit --no-edit` so `EDITOR=vim` does not open.

## Never run in agent shells

- `sudo` (e.g. `hosts` / `h` aliases)
- Interactive pagers or TUIs (`tig`, `less` on long git output without `--no-pager`)
- `brew_update` unless explicitly requested

## Drupal / DDEV

Use `ddev drush` and `ddev composer`, not host `drush` or `composer`.

## PATH / utilities

GNU coreutils are prepended in `~/.environment` (`gls`, etc.). `ls` is aliased to `gls` when available — do not assume BSD `ls` flags in portable scripts.

`direnv` is hooked in `~/.zshrc`; some project dirs may require `.envrc` — if direnv errors, note it rather than prompting.

## Stuck agent terminal

If a command waits for `[y/n]` or password input, the user cannot answer in a read-only agent terminal. Kill the stuck process (e.g. `rm -i`) from a separate shell instead of expecting Ctrl+C from the user.

## Cursor agent sessions

When `CURSOR_AGENT` is set, Powerlevel10k heavy prompt init is skipped (`~/.zshrc`) — normal for agent terminals.
